# --- GiGi development build ---
# The dev build runs with an in-memory store and needs NO secrets to boot,
# EXCEPT the beta code once it is deployed (see below).

# Beta gate (src/lib/beta.ts, src/middleware.ts). OPT-IN, and currently off.
#   • GIGI_BETA_GATE=on is the ONLY thing that raises the gate. Anything else,
#     unset included, and the site serves openly — which is how the build runs
#     on its *.vercel.app hostnames until a real domain is attached.
#   • GIGI_BETA_CODE is the code testers then type. Any string; compared case-
#     and whitespace-insensitively, and harmless to leave set while the gate is
#     down (a stale code cannot lock the build on its own).
#   • Gate ON with no code → every request gets a 503. That combination fails
#     CLOSED on purpose: having asked for a gate, a missing code is a mistake.
# Indexing is a SEPARATE switch (GIGI_SITE_ENV below). An ungated dev build is
# still noindex, and taking the gate off must never be what changes that.
# GIGI_BETA_GATE=
# GIGI_BETA_CODE=

# Which deployment this is. Only `production` is allowed to be indexed by
# search engines; anything else serves robots.txt with Disallow: / so
# dev.getgigiapp.com never turns up next to the real site.
GIGI_SITE_ENV=development

# Port is provided by Render automatically; only set locally if you want.
# PORT=3000

# Anthropic — set this to turn on the real Claude path:
#   • AI bill extraction (Prompt 1) on forwarded email
#   • the voice assistant (/app/voice)
#   • the extraction eval running against Claude (/app/eval)
# Without it, extraction uses the heuristic baseline and voice is disabled.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Anthropic inference region — see docs/DECISIONS.md (§4 / DPIA note).
# Lock inference to EU to keep "EU data only" true. Default eu.
# ANTHROPIC_REGION=eu

# Voice assistant model (defaults to claude-sonnet-5, the repo standard).
# GIGI_ASSISTANT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Supabase (Postgres) — swap the in-memory store for this when ready.
# See db/schema.sql for the schema.
# DATABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Default market for new households: uk | se  (see docs/DECISIONS.md §2)
# Drives currency and timezone for every household created from here on.
GIGI_DEFAULT_MARKET=uk

# --- Real accounts ----------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing key. Session cookies are SIGNED rather than looked up in a
# table, because the store below is in-memory: on Vercel every serverless
# instance has its own memory, so a session recorded in one instance stops
# resolving as soon as a request lands on another (src/lib/secrets.ts).
#   • Set this in production.
#   • Unset but GIGI_DEV_PASSWORD set → that is used as key material instead, so
#     working logins need one variable rather than two.
#   • Neither set → a per-process random key. Fine locally; on serverless every
#     login is lost. /api/auth/dev-users reports which of the three is in play.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# GIGI_SESSION_SECRET=

# Test accounts (src/lib/dev-users.ts). Derived from these variables rather than
# stored, so every instance computes the identical household — which is what
# makes logging in actually work on Vercel before the Postgres swap.
#   • UNSET ⇒ no test accounts exist at all. There is deliberately no default
#     password: a hardcoded one on a deployed build is a back door.
#   • Each test user is a normal owner of their own household with an EMPTY
#     register. /api/auth/demo still gives the pre-filled demo household.
# GIGI_DEV_PASSWORD=
# Optional. "email:Name, email:Name". Defaults to two accounts on example.com.
# GIGI_DEV_USERS=alpha@example.com:Alpha, beta@example.com:Beta

# --- Gmail OAuth (optional) — see docs/GMAIL_OAUTH.md -----------------------
# NOTE: Gmail needs an OAuth 2.0 *client*, not an API key. An API key cannot
# read a mailbox; users.messages.list answers 401 with one.
# Unset ⇒ the Connect-Gmail card shows "Unavailable" and forwarding is unaffected.
#
# gmail.readonly is one of Google's RESTRICTED scopes. In Testing mode (≤100
# test users) nothing needs verifying, but refresh tokens expire after 7 DAYS,
# so expect weekly re-consent. Publishing needs verification + a CASA
# assessment (6–10 weeks) — see docs/DECISIONS.md §1.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must match the redirect URI registered in Google Cloud Console byte for byte.
# Derived from the request when unset — fine locally, wrong on Vercel, where
# every preview deployment has a hostname Google has never heard of.
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-domain/api/auth/google/callback

# Inbound email webhook (forward feature) — see docs/FORWARDING.md.
# If set, POST /api/inbound requires this as an x-gigi-secret header or
# ?secret= query param, so a public URL can't be spammed.
# INBOUND_SECRET=
